The candidate text addresses the existence and review of a recovery plan (CIP-009 R1 territory), but says nothing about testing that plan on a 15-calendar-month cycle, which is what CIP-009-6 R2 Part 2.1 mandates. The governing requirement's core obligation — periodic testing via incident recovery, tabletop, or operational exercise — is entirely absent from the candidate language.

{"determination": "ABSENT", "cited_refs": ["CIP-009-6 R2 Part 2.1"], "rationale": "The candidate text only establishes that a documented OT BES Cyber System recovery plan exists and is reviewed when infrastructure changes occur, which speaks to CIP-009-6 R1 rather than R2. It contains no provision for testing the recovery plan at least once every 15 calendar months by incident recovery, paper/tabletop drill, or operational exercise, so the governing requirement's mandatory periodic-testing obligation is not addressed."}

DETERMINATION COMPLETE

